gomodel:6ab067da00000473
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "Built by claude4go 2026-09-23 from Brauer et al 2024 EMBO J (PMID:39587297, full text read). GOLPH3 and GOLPH3L are functionally redundant COPI adaptors that bind LYSET (co-IP of GOLPH3 with LYSET and with the LYSET-GNPTAB complex; AlphaFold contacts via LYSET R37/R39) and retain it in the Golgi; in GOLPH3/GOLPH3L double-KO (not single-KO) LYSET and GNPT are lost from the Golgi, degraded in lysosomes (rescued by bafilomycin/protease inhibitors), M6P tagging of soluble lysosomal enzymes fails and their immature precursors are hypersecreted; GOLPH3 WT but not the PI4P-binding mutant R90L rescues. LYSET is modelled as a molecular adaptor retaining/activating GNPTAB (Richards 2022 PMID:36074821, Pechincha 2022 PMID:36096887); GNPTAB is the catalytic subunit, part of the GNPT complex GO:0070622 (with GNPTG, PMID:26385638). Second branch: SPPL3 cleaves B4GALT5 off its membrane anchor and the soluble ectodomain is M6P-tagged (anti-M6P precipitation of B4GALT5-V5; absent in GNPTAB/LYSET KO) and sorted by the M6P receptor (ammonium chloride causes its secretion; SPPL3 KO and D271N abolish it). GOLPH3L edges are IGI with GOLPH3 (double vs single KO). IGF2R chosen as the MPR (CI-MPR-deficient mouse serum has soluble B4GALT5, Qian 2008 cited); M6PR likely redundant, not modelled. Lysosomal degradation of B4GALT5 is 'likely' per the authors and not modelled. GOLPH3->LYSET is 'indirectly positively regulates' (retention/level control, not catalysis); LYSET->GNPTAB is direct (physical complex)." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. GOLPH3 and GOLPH3L redundantly retain LYSET, and thereby the GNPT complex, in the Golgi, enabling mannose 6-phosphate tagging and MPR sorting of B4GALT5 after SPPL3 cleavage (Brauer 2024)." , "2026-10-20: B4GALT5 activity unit added earlier today removed again at curator request (no evidence for a causal link downstream of IGF2R). CTSL/HEXB removal kept." , "2026-10-20: CTSL and HEXB removed as inputs of GNPTAB and IGF2R; B4GALT5 kept as the only cargo input. Added B4GALT5 activity unit (GO:0008489; GlcCer CHEBI:22801 -> LacCer CHEBI:17950, both located in GO:0160289; part of GO:0001572), regulated by GOLPH3 (indirectly positively regulates, IMP PMID:33749896), as in gomodel:6ab067da00000385." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "production" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-23" ;
        dc:title               "M6P tagging via GOLPH3/GOLPH3L-retained LYSET-GNPT (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "https://www.uniprot.org" , "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00000473 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

